Original commit body from e89136f29bc0332d6d2beaf5146d3abdd688168d:

INV-rahib's residual class: 14 of 485 recorded runs ended with
_autopr_state_final still holding its "unknown" initializer, most recent
2026-09-11, one of them at exit 0. The owner ruling of 2026-08-03 makes
`unknown` the violation signal rather than a state, because no deliberate
exit writes it.

Two mechanisms, needing two different instruments.

Ten deliberate exits forgot to declare. The branch-ownership guards before
both amend paths, both re-push failures and both PR lookups inside stuck-CI
recovery, the simulated outage, and the unresolvable / non-linear vPR queue
checks. Each now names what it decided, and the four new states join the
declared closed set.

The enumeration is a dominance analysis, because proximity clears the real
cases: the assignment at auto-pr:2085 is in the `if _pre_scenario_b_gate`
arm while the exits at 2105/2114 are in the `else` arm. A 25-line distance
threshold hid 2105 outright while I was looking for these by hand.

The rest is a `set -e` abort at any unguarded command in a 700-line
function, which is not statically enumerable, so the run attributes itself.
auto-pr runs under errtrace with an ERR trap recording file:line and the
command; finalize prints a CONVERGENCE VIOLATION banner and persists
abort_site / abort_command to the sentinel and the ledger.

`-E` is load-bearing, not decoration. Without it an ERR trap is not
inherited by shell functions, and every real auto-pr abort happens inside a
helper. The first version of the behavioral test passed with `-E` removed,
because its fixture aborted in the same frame that installed the trap —
the harness contaminating its own control. The replacement aborts one call
deep and was verified by mutation.

Two gaps stay disclosed rather than counted as zero. A `set -u` unbound
variable does not fire ERR — bash raises it as an expansion error, not a
command failure — and neither does a bare `exit`. So the audit reports
three states, not two: a recorded site, "not recorded" (the trap could not
see it), and "not instrumented" (the row predates this change). A null
default would have merged the last two and reported the entire historical
backlog as live instrument failures.

BASH_COMMAND holds source text rather than its expansion, so a line
carrying $HG_GITHUB_TOKEN records the name. That is a property of bash, so
it is pinned by a test instead of asserted in a comment.

Also stops the rahib harness carrying its own copy of the shell flags; it
reads them from auto-pr now, which is what kept this file honest when `-E`
landed.

WI-nazoj, closed with evidence before this PR. Criterion (c) — re-measuring
the ledger over a comparable number of post-instrumentation runs — is filed
as WI-katap, since 485 rows took six weeks to accumulate.

